ComicCraft – AI Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models
Project Testing
1. Testing Overview
Testing is an important phase of the ComicCraft project to ensure that the application works correctly, generates usable AI content, protects user data, and provides a smooth comic-creation experience.
The testing process covers:
•	User interface
•	Authentication
•	Database
•	Backend APIs
•	Gemini AI integration
•	Comic generation
•	Comic editor
•	Image handling
•	Preview
•	Export
•	Security
•	Performance
•	End-to-end workflow
The overall testing process is:
Test Planning
     ↓
Unit Testing
     ↓
Integration Testing
     ↓
AI Testing
     ↓
System Testing
     ↓
Security Testing
     ↓
Performance Testing
     ↓
User Acceptance Testing
     ↓
Bug Fixing
     ↓
Final Validation
________________________________________
2. Testing Objectives
The main objectives are to:
1.	Verify that all functional requirements are implemented.
2.	Ensure users can create and manage comic projects.
3.	Verify Gemini generates valid and relevant comic content.
4.	Ensure AI-generated data is correctly stored.
5.	Verify users can edit generated comics.
6.	Ensure PDF/image exports are generated correctly.
7.	Identify and fix application errors.
8.	Verify unauthorized users cannot access other users' projects.
9.	Check application performance and reliability.
10.	Ensure the final system is suitable for real-world use.
________________________________________
3. Testing Strategy
ComicCraft uses several levels of testing.
Testing Type	Purpose
Unit Testing	Test individual functions/components
Integration Testing	Test interaction between modules
AI Testing	Test Gemini-generated content
